1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,840
Gus has a billion dollars, and

2
00:00:01,850 --> 00:00:03,380
he's running away from a snail.

3
00:00:03,424 --> 00:00:04,504
It's nine in the morning in

4
00:00:04,514 --> 00:00:06,004
the garden, and the deal is

5
00:00:06,014 --> 00:00:06,564
simple.

6
00:00:06,608 --> 00:00:07,528
He keeps the money.

7
00:00:07,768 --> 00:00:09,238
But a snail that can't die

8
00:00:09,248 --> 00:00:10,998
will follow him forever, and one

9
00:00:11,008 --> 00:00:12,398
touch means game over.

10
00:00:12,442 --> 00:00:13,202
His wife laughs.

11
00:00:13,212 --> 00:00:14,132
It's a snail.

12
00:00:14,372 --> 00:00:15,932
His neighbor steps right over it.

13
00:00:15,942 --> 00:00:16,932
Just walk away.

14
00:00:16,976 --> 00:00:17,926
And they've got a point.

15
00:00:18,196 --> 00:00:20,096
The fastest snail ever timed took

16
00:00:20,106 --> 00:00:21,966
two minutes to go thirteen inches.

17
00:00:22,010 --> 00:00:23,480
Gus takes one step and the

18
00:00:23,490 --> 00:00:25,160
snail needs four minutes to catch

19
00:00:25,170 --> 00:00:25,400
up.

20
00:00:25,454 --> 00:00:27,184
He walks almost five hundred times

21
00:00:27,194 --> 00:00:28,354
faster than it crawls.

22
00:00:28,398 --> 00:00:29,588
So why can't Gus sleep at

23
00:00:29,598 --> 00:00:29,918
night?

24
00:00:29,972 --> 00:00:31,262
You see, Gus has to stop.

25
00:00:31,272 --> 00:00:31,962
He eats.

26
00:00:31,992 --> 00:00:32,452
He naps.

27
00:00:32,462 --> 00:00:33,052
He sleeps.

28
00:00:33,062 --> 00:00:34,492
The snail never does.

29
00:00:34,536 --> 00:00:35,746
It's like a dripping tap.

30
00:00:36,056 --> 00:00:37,546
One drop is nothing, but leave

31
00:00:37,556 --> 00:00:38,616
it for a week and it

32
00:00:38,626 --> 00:00:39,886
fills a whole bathtub.

33
00:00:39,930 --> 00:00:41,920
Every night Gus sleeps, the snail

34
00:00:41,930 --> 00:00:43,770
gets eighty seven yards closer.

35
00:00:43,814 --> 00:00:45,414
That's two hundred and sixty yards

36
00:00:45,424 --> 00:00:47,204
a day, and fifty four miles

37
00:00:47,214 --> 00:00:47,674
a year.

38
00:00:47,728 --> 00:00:49,118
Luckily, Gus can win a whole

39
00:00:49,128 --> 00:00:50,348
day back with a three minute

40
00:00:50,358 --> 00:00:50,848
walk.

41
00:00:50,902 --> 00:00:52,612
And one flight across the ocean

42
00:00:52,622 --> 00:00:54,192
puts sixty four years between

43
00:00:54,202 --> 00:00:54,452
them.

44
00:00:54,506 --> 00:00:56,226
Unluckily, snails are very good at

45
00:00:56,236 --> 00:00:57,036
hitching a ride.

46
00:00:57,080 --> 00:00:58,230
So Gus lands on a sunny

47
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:00,110
beach with a billion dollars, one

48
00:01:00,120 --> 00:01:02,190
suitcase, and one very patient

49
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:02,980
snail.
